      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now Sarai, Abram's wife, bore him no children. She had an Egyptian maid whose name was Hagar; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and Sarai said to Abram, “Behold now, the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " has prevented me from bearing children; go in to my maid; it may be that I shall obtain children by her.” And Abram hearkened to the voice of Sarai. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So, after Abram had dwelt ten years in the land of Canaan, Sarai, Abram's wife, took Hagar the Egyptian, her maid, and gave her to Abram her husband as a wife. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he went in to Hagar, and she conceived; and when she saw that she had conceived, she looked with contempt on her mistress. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Sarai said to Abram, “May the wrong done to me be on you! I gave my maid to your embrace, and when she saw that she had conceived, she looked on me with contempt. May the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " judge between you and me!” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Abram said to Sarai, “Behold, your maid is in your power; do to her as you please.” Then Sarai dealt harshly with her, and she fled from her.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.6"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The angel of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " found her by a spring of water in the wilderness, the spring on the way to Shur. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he said, “Hagar, maid of Sarai, where have you come from and where are you going?” She said, “I am fleeing from my mistress Sarai.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The angel of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " said to her, “Return to your mistress, and submit to her.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The angel of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " also said to her, “I will so greatly multiply your descendants that they cannot be numbered for multitude.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the angel of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " said to her, “Behold, you are with child, and shall bear a son; you shall call his name Ishmael;",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16.11",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "That is",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "God hears",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " because the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " has given heed to your affliction. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He shall be a wild ass of a man, his hand against every man and every man's hand against him; and he shall dwell over against all his kinsmen.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So she called the name of the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " who spoke to her, “Thou art a God of seeing”; for she said, “Have I really seen God and remained alive after seeing him?”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16.13",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Cn: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "have I even here seen after him who sees me?",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "GEN 16:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Therefore the well was called Beer-lahai-roi;",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16.14",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "That is",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "the well of one who sees and lives",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " it lies between Kadesh and Bered.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "GEN.16.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "GEN.16.14"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
